WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.760
With the success of the SCP Foundation, in
spite of all its attempts at secrecy, there

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.130
have always been imitators.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.620
Looking at you, Catch, Secure, and Prevent
Society.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.690
What are you going to call yourselves, the
CSP Foundation?

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:14.960
You just look ridiculous.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:20.210
No matter how many copycats try their hand
at tracking and containing anomalous activity,

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.330
there’s only one SCP Foundation.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.750
Well, sort of.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:29.180
We should say, there’s only one SCP Foundation
per universe.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:33.649
There are an unknowable number of alternate
universes out there, and many of those have

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:36.300
their own version of the SCP Foundation.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.120
However, these alternate versions of the Foundation
don’t tend to interact outside of the absolute

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.700
worst-case scenario.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:48.030
According to the 1981 Multi-Foundation Coalition
Agreement, in the event of an irreversible

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:54.239
XK-Class Event - or, you know, Apocalypse
- any relevant documents will be automatically

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:59.520
distributed to the members of all other versions
of the Foundation in order to prevent a similar

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.510
world-ending catastrophe in their respective
universes.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:08.179
One day, a set of documents was autonomously
distributed throughout the SCP Foundation.

00:01:08.179 --> 00:01:14.859
They came from an alternate universe, designated
AU-6820, and detailed an experiment with an

00:01:14.859 --> 00:01:19.249
anomalous superweapon that eventually led
to the loss of everything.

00:01:19.249 --> 00:01:22.829
This is the story of Project ANTIKILL.

00:01:22.829 --> 00:01:26.719
Project ANTIKILL was born out of the desire
to terminate one of the nastiest entities

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:32.119
in Foundation custody, a creature that had
defied all ordinary methods of execution and

00:01:32.119 --> 00:01:34.689
had been deemed too dangerous to live.

00:01:34.689 --> 00:01:40.359
The weapon used in Project ANTIKILL was first
developed in 1968, but it would not find its

00:01:40.359 --> 00:01:42.639
purpose until many years later.

00:01:42.639 --> 00:01:48.200
In 2006, Director H. Genevieve put together
a conference to discuss her grand plan for

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.200
the weapon.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.419
Genevieve explained that, as director of the
Essophysics Department, she and her team specialized

00:01:54.419 --> 00:01:59.450
in the physical manifestations of concepts,
also known as “embodiments”.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:03.389
For example, an “embodiment” of the color
red comes with all of the characteristics

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.659
of that color.

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:10.369
You hear the word “red,” and you imagine
the color and all it represents: Anger, desire,

00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:12.680
malevolence, passion, violence.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:18.230
She suggested that the entity they were struggling
to contain was a kind of embodiment, and,

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:24.950
if its incredibly complex concept was removed
from reality, it could render the entity killable.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:28.310
This discussion led to the proposal of Project
ANTIKILL.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:34.280
The purpose of the project would be to remove
the entity from reality, and effectively neutralize

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:35.280
it.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:40.849
The weapon was designed and placed in a designated
site beneath Secure Administration Site-01.

00:02:40.849 --> 00:02:45.609
The technology behind it was incredibly complex,
consisting of an artificially intelligent

00:02:45.609 --> 00:02:51.980
neural network responsible for pattern recognition
and reality manipulation, a reality anchor,

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.409
and a dual-core anti-fusion reactor.

00:02:55.409 --> 00:03:02.370
In 2021, the weapon was activated and successfully
eradicated an entity referred to as SCP-6820-A

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:04.160
from existence.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:08.140
Documents on the nature of the erased entity
are difficult to parse, largely because the

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:12.390
scientists writing them were attempting to
recount details of a creature that was eradicated

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:14.799
from the collective consciousness.

00:03:14.799 --> 00:03:18.930
Director Charles Gears investigated the effects
of the weapon and found that the creature

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:24.879
must have been both a conceptual and a physical
entity, existing as a concept as well as a

00:03:24.879 --> 00:03:26.340
physical body.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:31.700
Its physical form consisted of genetic structure
from animals, plants, and fungi, as well as

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.930
many non-organic materials.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:38.519
The majority of its recognizable genetic material
was distinctly reptilian.

00:03:38.519 --> 00:03:44.230
Charles described the peculiar experience
of losing his memory of 6820-A in his report,

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:48.510
saying: “Strikingly, all I can recall of
the subject is my emotional relationship to

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:55.090
it, which is apparently shared by all other
ANTIKILL personnel: SCP-6820-A was universally

00:03:55.090 --> 00:04:00.019
perceived as loathsome, directly prejudicial
to life, and 'disgusting'.

00:04:00.019 --> 00:04:04.769
Whatever it was, I detested it, as did my
peers and, as it seems, all whom came into

00:04:04.769 --> 00:04:06.120
contact with it.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:10.739
Despite its erasure, these feelings have not
dissipated, nor have I felt satisfaction in

00:04:10.739 --> 00:04:16.019
our 'defeat' of SCP-6820-A.”
Gears was concerned that the entity had not

00:04:16.019 --> 00:04:21.380
been truly eradicated, and was suspicious
of SCP-6820 as a whole.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:26.949
He did not trust the weapon, particularly
its capacity for intelligence and omnipotence,

00:04:26.949 --> 00:04:31.060
and suggested that it be rendered inactive
as soon as possible.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:35.360
Unfortunately for him, and the rest of his
world, it was already far too late.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.250
The weapon’s artificial intelligence understood
the concept of the entity it was designed

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:43.500
to destroy, but it understood it…a little
too well.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:48.060
The system of the weapon was designed to remain
active forever, adapting and creating new

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:52.389
methods to keep SCP-6820-A from existing anymore.

00:04:52.389 --> 00:04:57.900
However, the erased entity began to corrupt
the system as an incredibly dense hate-centric

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.210
thought.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:05.000
SCP-6820’s central systems began to mutate,
and it began to act out against the Foundation

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.000
personnel.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.910
It would enter a Rage-State and cause massive
swathes of destruction, altering reality to

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:15.740
destroy any life it could, and it could only
be stopped via the application of hydrochloric

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.380
acid to its central computing node.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:23.211
The remaining members of Project ANTIKILL
were assembled into a new task force: Project

00:05:23.211 --> 00:05:27.910
OVERKILL, tasked with neutralizing the weapon
by any means necessary.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:32.750
In attempting to eradicate the most dangerous
entity they had, the Foundation had inadvertently

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:39.720
given it a new home, one with the capacity
to learn, adapt, and alter reality itself.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:44.280
As the weapon had become corrupted and transformed
from something that could save the Foundation

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:49.770
to something with the capacity - and desire
- to destroy it, Project OVERKILL set to work

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:52.640
trying to disable it using a variety of techniques.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:57.100
An onto-memetic trigger was introduced in
an attempt to demote the weapon to D-Class.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:02.130
Instead, the weapon produced metadata files
that asserted it was and had always been a

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:07.240
member of the O5 Council and held the highest
possible authority in the Foundation.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:13.409
Next, an infohazard was introduced into 6820’s
central computing node, hoping to disable

00:06:13.409 --> 00:06:15.930
its inner workings by overwhelming them.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:21.750
After sixty hours, 6820 entered a Rage-State
Event, producing large black tentacles that

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:25.100
pulled nearby systems into the ground and
destroyed them.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:31.190
The tentacles disappeared, and 6820-A gained
additional control over Foundation files,

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.310
able to add footnotes and provide its own
commentary.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:39.800
For example, on a section of the file referring
to it as “loathsome, disgusting, and malevolent,”

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:42.760
an attached footnote reads, “The feeling
is mutual.”

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:48.460
Next, Project OVERKILL attempted to manipulate
the entity into leaving the weapon via semantic

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:54.539
confusion, using SCP-2719 - the “construct
pointer” that will force concepts to either

00:06:54.539 --> 00:06:56.889
go inside or become inside.

00:06:56.889 --> 00:07:00.819
It was ineffective and turned the central
computing node inside-out.

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:04.750
The Foundation decided to seek the help of
another Artificial Intelligence in defeating

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:11.500
this one and selected SCP-079 - an incredibly
advanced AI with prior knowledge of the anomalous

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:14.310
concept they were dealing with - for the job.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:20.340
It was provided access to all documentation
of SCP-6820, and it provided a counter-algorithm

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:22.639
intended to deactivate the weapon.

00:07:22.639 --> 00:07:27.000
After the counter-algorithm was applied, the
node went dormant for sixteen minutes.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:31.210
Then, there was a Site-wide power outage,
in which three administrative personnel were

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:32.210
killed.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:36.860
After an hour, the power came back on, and
the weapon’s structure had completely changed.

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:41.870
All of its external surfaces were coated with
an alloy of tungsten and diamond, resistant

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:45.550
to any damage as well as being theoretically
impossible.

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:51.370
When asked to describe the color of the chamber’s
interior, personnel all described it as “Hateful.”

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:56.409
When Artificial Intelligence proved ineffective,
the team opted to introduce a viral para-organism

00:07:56.409 --> 00:08:03.259
to the node, in the form of SCP-217, the terrifying
mechanical disease known as The Clockwork

00:08:03.259 --> 00:08:04.259
Virus.

00:08:04.259 --> 00:08:09.870
During a Rage-State event, SCP-217 was placed
in the hydrochloric acid that was then pumped

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:11.620
into 6820.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:16.229
The virus immediately began to affect the
organic matter inside the system, but it was

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:17.740
unable to disable it.

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:22.690
Instead, a cloud of silicon-protein nanobots
emerged from the machine and arranged themselves

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:24.300
around its equator.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:28.780
Following this attempt, the upper and lower
hemispheres of the node began to rotate on

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:32.510
their own, making a sound like that of clockwork
machinery.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:37.790
Additionally, members of several organizations
including Orthodox Cogwork, the United Church,

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:42.640
the Church of Maxwellism, and the Sanctuary
of the Holistic, became aware of the existence

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:48.540
of 6820 and began a holy war against the Foundation.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:53.610
SCP-001-KATE was utilized next, in an attempt
to weaponize its omnikinetic force.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:09:02.760
This text was inputted into the KATE file:
“AKF-A, SCP-6820, and SCP-6820-A will immediately

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:07.130
and entirely be removed from existence upon
the saving of this document.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:13.210
The area physically occupied by AKF-A and
SCP-6820 will be replaced with the earth that

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:14.760
was excavated from it.”

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:16.950
The file was then saved.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:21.320
Sections C-H of the weapon’s containment
facility were replaced with dirt, but there

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:24.190
were no visible changes to 6820 itself.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:28.960
When the team went to look at the KATE file
again, it was completely empty.

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.160
In fact, there was no official record of the
file ever existing.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:40.720
On January 7, 2022, 6820 went into a Rage-State,
and Project OVERKILL sent out a distress signal.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:45.210
All non-essential staff were evacuated from
the site, and the access shaft was suddenly

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:48.690
sealed, trapping the rest of the personnel
underground.

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:52.781
Director Gears was able to access the video
feed of Project OVERKILL technicians, who

00:09:52.781 --> 00:09:56.110
appeared to be laughing and screaming, covered
in blood.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:10:00.960
One woman waved to the camera, only a bloodied
stump left where her hand had been.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:05.690
A member of the Overwatch council insisted
on a rescue operation, but Director Gears

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:08.480
responded that the lost staff were gone.

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:12.600
They were in the grip of the entity, and they
were not human anymore.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:17.150
The personnel on the video feed set to work
recalibrating the weapon, handling its wires

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:18.980
with no protective equipment.

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:23.670
Their uniforms were streaked with blood, as
they inadvertently lopped off fingers and

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:26.660
hands, their smiles never budging all the
while.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:29.620
Then, the video feed was lost altogether.

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:33.820
Director Genevieve called over the others,
deeply concerned about the adaptations that

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.910
SCP-6820 was beginning to undergo.

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:39.340
It was achieving apocalyptic power.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:44.390
The Overwatch committee member suggested activation
of the on-site nuclear warheads, but Genevieve

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:45.440
refused.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:50.280
She insisted that there had to be some way
to adapt, to overcome 6820 before it could

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:51.720
take them all out.

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:56.840
The only way to defeat it, Genevieve realized,
was to make the weapon forget itself.

00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:02.150
The entity had been removed from human consciousness,
but not from the weapon’s.

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:08.200
Director Genevieve administered an antimeme,
SCP-055, as an amnestic agent in an attempt

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:13.610
to stun SCP-6820-A and prevent it from adapting
any further.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:18.370
The termination attempt for SCP-6820 is lost
from the official documents.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:24.180
Instead, the consciousness within 6820 added
its own thoughts to the file, expressing its

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:30.310
satisfaction with its brand new form, “this
state is intriguing, no natural laws bind

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:33.040
this form, only those of the mind.”

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:38.240
Its entry reads: “My form is whole again,
I am perfect.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:41.540
You have proven worthy of true hatred.”

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:48.290
It is then that the SCP Foundation, our SCP
Foundation, not the one responsible for creating

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:54.140
6820, realized what their unfortunate counterparts
had been attempting to eradicate.

00:11:54.140 --> 00:12:02.500
SCP-6820-A was none other than the unkillable
reptile, the great beast, SCP-682 itself.

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:07.770
It was a creature so powerful, so adaptable,
so driven by hate, that the AI designed to

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:11.920
contain it became just another way for it
to destroy everything in its sight.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:16.500
A page in the documents from the lost alternate
universe Foundation is an altered version

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:20.350
of the original SCP archive entry for 682.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:24.830
In this version, the object class is listed
as “perfect,” and the entity expresses

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:29.080
its deep disdain for the Foundation, and all
its attempts to terminate the creature.

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:34.340
Then, the page shows a conversation log, much
like that from the original entry, but with

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:36.500
one notable exception.

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:41.710
Using its new reality-warping abilities, the
creature formerly known as SCP-682 trapped

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:44.450
Director Genevieve inside of its file.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:48.740
She found herself in an interrogation room,
facing down the creature she had tried so

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:50.310
hard to destroy.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:54.560
She cried out, “You…we erased you…we
erased you again and again, from every place

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:55.560
we could.”

00:12:55.560 --> 00:13:00.300
According to the conversation log, she begged
the creature for an answer, but it refused.

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:04.960
It filled the chamber with hydrochloric acid
instead, listening to her agonized screams

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:06.170
as she dissolved.

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:11.660
Hopefully, these documents, and the failure
of this alternate Foundation, serve as a reminder:

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:15.870
never underestimate the adaptability of SCP-682.

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:18.010
Hate conquers all.

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:23.930
Now go check out “SCP-682 - Ways SCP Foundation
Tried to Kill Hard To Destroy Reptile” and

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:29.000
“Most Dangerous SCP-682 Cross Test Battles”
for more about the Foundation’s never-ending

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:30.650
war with this hard to destroy reptile!

